WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- Thank you.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.880
- Y'all look so fabulous right now.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.579
Both of you complimenting each other.

00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:05.412
- You guys look beautiful.

00:00:05.412 --> 00:00:06.280
- It's like you're in a video.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:07.113
- We are working it.

00:00:07.113 --> 00:00:07.946
- Looks beautiful.

00:00:07.946 --> 00:00:09.720
- So last time you were here,

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.680
you were going to college, right?

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:11.513
You were on your way?

00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:12.346
- I was on the way to college.

00:00:12.346 --> 00:00:13.179
- [Kelly] Is it USC?

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.190
- I'm at USC.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.023
- [Kelly] How's it going?

00:00:15.023 --> 00:00:15.856
- It's so good.

00:00:15.856 --> 00:00:17.760
I'm in my sophomore year, second semester.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.113
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:19.113 --> 00:00:19.946
- I've been very busy.

00:00:19.946 --> 00:00:22.154
I missed the first part
of my first semester.

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:23.245
- [Kelly] Because of Covid.

00:00:23.245 --> 00:00:24.210
- Because of Covid

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.100
and like working and
things of that nature.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.330
But I just can't wait to be back

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.010
and I mean it's very important

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.980
for me to not only pursue my acting career

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.620
but furthering my education
is very important.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.288
So I'm glad that I just
could balance both.

00:00:37.288 --> 00:00:38.227
(people clap)

00:00:38.227 --> 00:00:39.997
- Well that's an
incredibly hard thing to do

00:00:39.997 --> 00:00:41.128
to balance both.

00:00:41.128 --> 00:00:41.961
- Yes. It is.

00:00:41.961 --> 00:00:42.794
- I think going to school too,

00:00:42.794 --> 00:00:44.040
it only helps you with acting

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.032
and then acting only helps,
so all of that can help you.

00:00:47.032 --> 00:00:47.865
- Exactly. It all informs each other.

00:00:47.865 --> 00:00:49.528
All helps each other.

00:00:49.528 --> 00:00:50.361
- Yeah, agreed.

00:00:50.361 --> 00:00:51.352
- Well I mentioned Euphoria,

00:00:51.352 --> 00:00:52.185
which you starred with Zendaya

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.280
and I didn't know this

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.110
but the first time you met her,

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.232
we found this picture.

00:00:56.232 --> 00:00:57.671
Look at her in this photo.

00:00:57.671 --> 00:00:59.310
- [Storm] I was a baby.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:00.143
- [Kelly] She is a baby.

00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:02.983
- [Marcia] Oh my God baby, baby, baby.

00:01:02.983 --> 00:01:06.270
- [Kelly] I mean, what kinda
life do you have to where

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.950
you meet her as a young

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.180
and then now you've worked with her?

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:10.620
- It's wild.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.724
It's a blessing.

00:01:11.724 --> 00:01:12.834
- [Kelly] That's crazy.

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.460
- Yeah. That was at the
Ben and Jerry's in Burbank.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:15.604
I was on the way.

00:01:15.604 --> 00:01:16.631
- First of all nice choice.

00:01:16.631 --> 00:01:17.464
- Yeah!

00:01:17.464 --> 00:01:18.297
- Half-Baked my favorite.

00:01:18.297 --> 00:01:19.130
- [Storm] Exactly.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:19.963
- [Kelly] Nice.

00:01:19.963 --> 00:01:21.720
- I was there. I was
about to go to the AMC

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.400
and I heard a familiar voice.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.110
And you know when you
hear a familiar voice

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.160
you turn around.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.710
I was ordering my ice
cream and then I just look

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.210
over my shoulder and she's right there.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.640
And I literally stood there
for probably about two minutes

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:33.660
and I was just like.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.640
And my mom was like,
"You're being embarrassing.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.200
You're either gonna go say hi

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.280
or don't say anything at all."

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.020
And now we're like, she's my big sis.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:40.980
We get to work together.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.630
And I just admire and love her.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.700
- I just love that. That is, you know,

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.980
sometimes we can harp on this city

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:48.540
for a lot of things that aren't great

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.330
but it's a beautiful
dreamer's place, you know?

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:52.561
It is.

00:01:52.561 --> 00:01:53.394
- [Storm] Absolutely.

00:01:53.394 --> 00:01:54.227
- [Kelly] It's really cool

00:01:54.227 --> 00:01:55.624
that you dream like
that when you're a kid.

00:01:55.624 --> 00:01:56.457
You have this goal,

00:01:56.457 --> 00:01:57.290
you meet this person that inspires you

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:58.123
and you end up working.

00:01:58.123 --> 00:01:58.956
That's a really cool story.

00:01:58.956 --> 00:02:00.040
- Exactly. It's very cool.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:00.873
(people cheer)

00:02:00.873 --> 00:02:02.070
- So I heard Storm that you
bought your mama a house.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.353
- I did.

00:02:03.353 --> 00:02:04.186
- How did that feel?

00:02:04.186 --> 00:02:05.019
- Oh, it was so good

00:02:05.019 --> 00:02:05.880
It feels so good.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.680
- I imagine, because
you're a young actress

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.660
so she probably had to
sacrifice quite a bit.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:10.493
- Absolutely.

00:02:10.493 --> 00:02:13.123
My mom has made so many sacrifices for me.

00:02:13.123 --> 00:02:13.956
There we are.

00:02:13.956 --> 00:02:15.480
She's made so many sacrifices for me.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.910
So to be able to come to LA from Atlanta,

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:18.900
we didn't have much.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.030
And to build the house in California.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:21.863
- [Marcia] Yeah.

00:02:21.863 --> 00:02:24.180
- It's a surreal experience

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.010
and something that I'm still processing

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.480
and trying to be grateful for.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.430
But I think it's also a really cool thing

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.314
where I get to pat myself on the back.

00:02:31.314 --> 00:02:32.147
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:02:32.147 --> 00:02:34.020
- And just see my mom happy
and renovate and decorate.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.900
She's like in her element,
living her best life.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.250
So it makes me happy.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.392
- That's just the coolest
thing be able to do.

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:41.370
(people clap)

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.260
- What was your favorite thing that

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.370
you maybe bought your mom?

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.710
- Oh I took mine both on
a trip to New Zealand.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:47.556
- [Kelly] Oh, that's incredible.

00:02:47.556 --> 00:02:49.350
- And so memories have become
a really important part

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.190
for me and my mom.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.950
My mother passed from
Alzheimer's and one of the things

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:56.323
I bought for her before she
passed was an Aura frame.

00:02:56.323 --> 00:02:57.156
And I literally should be the spokesperson

00:02:57.156 --> 00:02:57.989
for Aura frames.

00:02:57.989 --> 00:02:59.784
- Is that the one that
rotates the pictures?

00:02:59.784 --> 00:03:01.944
- Yes. And anybody can
email their pictures,

00:03:01.944 --> 00:03:03.360
the family can all email.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.980
And so she would have
all these familiar faces

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.300
all the time passing through.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.410
- That's kind of an
incredible gift for someone

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.840
with dementia to always be
reminded of these faces.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:10.673
- Yes, to be reminded.

00:03:10.673 --> 00:03:11.843
Even if she didn't always know,

00:03:11.843 --> 00:03:12.920
I remember once she said to me,

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:13.753
"I don't know who you are,

00:03:13.753 --> 00:03:14.670
but I know you're important to me."

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.670
And you're like, "That's
all you need to know Mom."

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.503
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:03:18.503 --> 00:03:19.336
- Important to you.

00:03:19.336 --> 00:03:20.820
But now I'm a little upset
I didn't buy her a house.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.120
- [Storm] Awe.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:22.953
(people laugh)

00:03:22.953 --> 00:03:24.301
- Yeah, you took her to New Zealand.

00:03:24.301 --> 00:03:25.134
- [Marcia] I did.

00:03:25.134 --> 00:03:25.967
- Also just made me cry.

00:03:25.967 --> 00:03:26.800
So you're doing fine.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:27.633
- [Marcia] It was such a beautiful time.

00:03:27.633 --> 00:03:29.760
- So your new movie also deals

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.770
with a mother-daughter relationship.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:32.610
It's called Missing.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:33.840
So can you tell everybody about it?

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.252
- Yes. So I have a movie,
Missing, where I play June.

00:03:37.252 --> 00:03:40.170
A stubborn young teenage girl

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.520
just really trying to figure out life.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.353
Who she want to be.

00:03:42.353 --> 00:03:43.897
- Never met one.

00:03:43.897 --> 00:03:45.556
Never been one.

00:03:45.556 --> 00:03:46.389
(people laugh)

00:03:46.389 --> 00:03:48.150
- So she's just really
trying to figure out life.

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:50.430
And her mom, Grace, goes on vacation

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.260
to Colombia with her boyfriend

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.700
and ends up going missing.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.830
So June has to try to figure

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:59.220
out where her mother is through
technology and social media.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:00.900
And it's different from any type of,

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.170
I guess other mysterious crime movie.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.820
Because it's all taking place

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:08.190
through my POV on computer screens.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.830
So you never actually
leave the computer screen

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.355
while you're watching this movie.

00:04:12.355 --> 00:04:13.240
- That's interesting.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.990
- Yeah. It was technically challenging.

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.370
Just the different eye lines

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.890
and filming on a phone
and computer and a watch.

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.099
Which is crazy to me.

00:04:21.099 --> 00:04:23.040
But it was a lot of fun.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:23.873
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:23.873 --> 00:04:26.910
So is your mom in real
life good with tech?

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.250
- I think she wishes she was better.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.120
She's not bad.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.557
- That means that means not good.

00:04:31.557 --> 00:04:32.390
(people laugh)

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.443
- No, it was just a big no.

00:04:33.443 --> 00:04:34.950
- Yeah. That's a hard no.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.230
- The emails, the phone calls, the texts,

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:38.700
she's got it all covered.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:39.930
And like the DocuSigns.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.660
Anything where she has to be in work mode,

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.670
she's got. But the Instagram

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:47.064
and anything other than work stuff.

00:04:47.064 --> 00:04:48.840
She's like, "Storm help me."

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.350
And it's just one button and
I'm like, "Here you go mom."

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.723
- It's not just one button, Storm.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:56.543
- I'm sorry.

00:04:56.543 --> 00:04:57.870
- Coming from other mothers

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:58.860
- And the remote,

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.995
they make the little icons this big.

00:05:00.995 --> 00:05:03.720
I'm like, what is it?
What does it say to do?

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.250
I can't see the damn thing.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.504
- Why do you need three?

00:05:06.504 --> 00:05:07.530
- [Marcia] Why?

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.730
- I got in, they installed it

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:11.460
and I'm just like there
are three remotes here.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:12.293
- [Marcia] Right.

00:05:12.293 --> 00:05:13.470
- What the hell are they all for?

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.320
- I had to call my son
from dance class one time,

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.360
he was in school, away
in a boarding school.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.927
I had to call him from dance class and say

00:05:19.927 --> 00:05:22.643
"How do you turn the TV on Hudson Shield?"

00:05:22.643 --> 00:05:23.476
(people laugh)

00:05:23.476 --> 00:05:24.684
- He was like, "Mom!"

00:05:24.684 --> 00:05:25.800
- And you're like, "I'm being serious.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.501
Tell me you're not getting off the phone."

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:28.334
- I'm serious.

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:29.167
That's right. That's exactly true.

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:30.000
- It's hard sometimes.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.951
I mean, not for me. I'm so good at this.

00:05:32.951 --> 00:05:35.010
Let's see a clip of the movie.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:37.169
Here is Storm Reid in Missing.

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:39.352
(phone rings)

00:05:39.352 --> 00:05:41.765
- [Nia] Siri. Call June.

00:05:41.765 --> 00:05:43.170
- [Storm] Oh my gosh, Mom.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.090
- [Nia] Siri please call June Bug.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:47.100
- [Storm] Mom you're already
on the phone this is FaceTime.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:47.940
- Oh gosh.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.350
- You know you don't have to use Siri

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:50.640
for literally everything right?

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.590
- Listen, I need you to write
a couple of things down.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.960
The car keys are going
to be in the top drawer

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.322
in the kitchen. And Kevin...

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:59.373
I just said write it down.
You're not writing it down.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:02.862
No alcohol and keep your location service

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:06.930
turned on the entire time I'm away.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.370
Do you understand?

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.013
- No fun, got it.

00:06:10.013 --> 00:06:11.731
(people clap and cheering)

00:06:11.731 --> 00:06:12.564
- The best part.

00:06:12.564 --> 00:06:13.740
Z U F Y

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.913
- Wasn't even typing anything.

00:06:14.913 --> 00:06:16.980
- Yeah, got it. Clear.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.680
Missing is now in theaters
and Marcia's film,

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.193
Daughter of the Bride, comes
out February 3rd y'all.

